<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mirza Ghalib</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1797–1869</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Asadullah Khan Ghalib</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mirza Ghalib was the leading <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/urdu">Urdu</a> and Persian poet of the late Mughal era, best known for his ghazals. Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agra">Agra</a>, he lived most of his life in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a>, married into the family of the nawabs of Loharu, and served as poet to the last Mughal emperor, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahadur-shah-ii">Bahadur Shah Zafar</a>. His letters and his account of 1857 record the destruction of Delhi after the Indian Rebellion.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mirza-ghalib.jpg" alt="Mirza Ghalib" width="290" height="462" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mirza_Ghalib_photograph_3.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
